Downloads Browser
=================

The web interface now includes a Downloads item in the left navigation,
between Manage Subscriptions and Settings. It provides read-only folder
browsing, displays file sizes, and lets users download files. In Docker
deployments, the UI mounts the configured downloads directory read-only at
CONTAINER_DATA_PATH (normally /data). The file endpoint rejects paths that
escape the downloads root.

The browser also supports recursive filename search across download folders
and a toggle between newest-first and oldest-first ordering by modification
time. Search results now include an explicit Clear search button, and the sort
button uses named callbacks to rerender the list with the selected order. Its
label describes the sort order that clicking it will select.
The same sort toggle orders folders by their modification time too, while
keeping folders grouped before files.

The search controls are compact icon buttons with tooltips, and the search can
also be submitted by pressing Enter.

The Downloads search input uses Quasar's borderless mode and CSS overrides
after the shared input styles so no border appears, including on focus.

The search controls are constrained to a single grid row, and all nested
search-field elements suppress the shared border, shadow, and focus outline.

